Every square matrix $matbold(M)$ with real entries decomposes as $matbold(M) = matbold(S) + matbold(A)$, where
$ matbold(S) = (1)/(2) (matbold(M) + matbold(M)^tp) quad "and" quad matbold(A) = (1)/(2) (matbold(M) - matbold(M)^tp) $
are the symmetric and antisymmetric parts. Since $tr(matbold(A)) = 0$ and $tr(matbold(S)) = tr(matbold(M))$, the symmetric part further splits into the traceless symmetric matrix $matbold(T) = matbold(S) - (1)/(n) tr(matbold(S)) matbold(I)$, with $tr(matbold(T)) = 0$, together with the isotropic part $(1)/(n) tr(matbold(M)) matbold(I)$:
$ matbold(M) = underbracket(matbold(T), "symmetric" \ "traceless") + underbracket((1)/(n) tr(matbold(M)) matbold(I), "isotropic part") + underbracket(matbold(A), "antisymmetric part"). $
